<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="99a055b6">&lt;p&gt;
    Strategic direction provides the long-term (3-5 year), broad, overarching approach to accomplish the vision or goals of
    an organization. This direction is expressed through a set of strategy statements with supporting tactics and
    associated critical success factors. Tactics, are focused, short-term activities specifically created and selected to
    reach specific and measurable objectives. Critical success factors (CSF) identify those contributing elements that must
    also go well in order for an organization to succeed in executing its strategy. They provide a more holistic viewpoint
    and approach for actively managing the strategic direction of the enterprise. Example: Our EY Vision 2020 strategy
    includes the strategy statement: “Relentless focus on the market”. One of its supporting strategies/tactics is a “Focus
    on Sectors”. An associated CSF would be “Develop, acquire, and retain people with deep sector experience and insight”.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="f9eb0db2"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="bc95f952">This work product will often be combined with others, such as goals and objectives, as part of a larger deliverable.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="5f90baa4"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="3a50ccac">To provide overarching guidance to the actions of an organization in terms of how it will achieve its mission.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="8c23cd85"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="a38982d4"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="725bf360">&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Strategy statement(s)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Tactic(s)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Critical success factor(s)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</attribute>
